%!PS-Adobe-3.0
%%Title: Released in Part -- a typed 1962 memo, copied and released decades later
%%BoundingBox: 0 0 612 792
%%EndComments

% A one-page office memorandum from an invented survey office, typed on a
% worn elite manual, then aged, folded, punched, stamped, annotated, redacted
% and photocopied for release. Every name, office, project and place in it is
% made up.
%
%   lib/typewriter.ps  tw-type: the memo header, tab stops, strikeover <o>,
%                      x-out <x>, underscore <u> and redaction <r> markup, and
%                      the ribbon ink (weave voids, feathered edges, clogged
%                      counters, a heavy side, light strikes)
%   lib/released.ps    rel-page: aged paper, folds, punch holes, the scanner's
%                      tilt and lamp, a photocopy generation (the type's
%                      counters close and its strokes thicken), stamps, a
%                      margin note and marker redaction bars
%
%   pscat --page 612x792 --png released_memo.png gallery/released_memo.ps
%   gs -q -dNOSAFER -dBATCH -dNOPAUSE -sDEVICE=png16m -r144 -g1224x1584 \
%      -dGraphicsAlphaBits=4 -dTextAlphaBits=4 \
%      -sOutputFile=released_memo_gs.png gallery/released_memo.ps </dev/null

(lib/artkit.ps) run
(lib/surfacekit.ps) run
(lib/handscript.ps) run
(lib/typewriter_outlines.ps) run
(lib/typewriter.ps) run
(lib/released.ps) run

1 setgray clippath fill

% rm- prefix: piece-local.
/rmtext (1.\tOn the morning of October 29 the Harlan Flats station reported that two cans of exposed film from the August flights over Section 9 could not be found. The cans were logged into the vault on September 4 by <r>Mr. R. T. Ashdown</r> and were last seen there on October 12, when the vault was opened for the quarterly count.

2.\tA search of the vault, the drying room and the mail cage has turned up nothing. The film itself is <u>not</u> restricted, but the flight sheets packed in the same cans <o>was|were</o> marked for office use only, and they show the survey lines for the reservoir site.

3.\tI have asked <r>the station chief</r> for a written account by November 16. Until the cans are found, no film is to leave the vault without two signatures in the log, <u>without exception</u>.

4.\tThe enclosed list gives the frame numbers of the <x>sixty</x> forty-two frames that cannot be flown again this season. The rest can be reflown in the spring if they must be.

5.\tPlease treat this matter as closed to inquiries from outside the office until the Division has replied.



\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tE. W. Marchetti
\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tActing Director

EWM:dlk
Enclosure) def

{
    <<
        /Text rmtext
        /Width 612 /Height 792 /Margin 72 /MarginTop 84
        /Pitch 12 /Size 11.5 /Tabs 5
        /Machine 11 /Seed 1962 /Wear 1.3 /MachineWear 0.6
        /Ink [0.17 0.16 0.17] /Ribbon 0.55 /Copies 0.35
        /Memo << /Title (MEMORANDUM)
                 /To (Chief, Records Division)
                 /From (Acting Director, Upper Basin Survey Office)
                 /Cc (Field Station 4, Harlan Flats)
                 /Subject (Loss of aerial film, Project GREYWING)
                 /Date (November 9, 1962) >>
